WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.320
Bard.

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:08.233
Witch.

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:09.700
What are you doing here?

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:15.166
And what fresh hell
did you just crawl out of?

00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:16.800
A sewer.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.733
What's your excuse?

00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:22.226
Oh, a sewer, I always knew you
were a blood sucking joyless…

00:00:22.226 --> 00:00:24.186
hugger.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.433
One of my favourite things
about shooting Season 2

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:33.533
was the fact that I got
to work with Anya again.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.933
Witches are bound to bump
into monsters eventually.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.733
Jaskier.

00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:39.653
Yennefer.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.980
Oh, she’s so scary.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.066
They’re frenemies,
first and foremost.

00:00:47.066 --> 00:00:48.706
That’s what we discover
in Season 1 anyway.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.620
I hate to break it to you,
but that ship has sailed,

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.800
wrecked, and sunk to
the bottom of the ocean.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.300
Ow.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.233
In Season 2, they’ve both lost
someone very important to them

00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:01.366
and I think that really connects them.

00:01:01.366 --> 00:01:02.766
We’re better off without him.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.460
Anya and I are good pals

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.133
and we get on really, really well

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.366
and by the time the scripts landed

00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:13.433
and we saw we had
a lot more to do together,

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:18.193
we really wanted to dive into
what made these characters tick

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.240
and why this unlikely reunion came about.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.400
I would not wish that fate
on my worst enemy

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.800
and yes you are…
firmly lodged in that category,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.600
it has to be said.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.560
It feels light-hearted with Jaskier.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.673
They just enjoy
playing with each other. 

00:01:32.673 --> 00:01:34.900
You both smell truly awful.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:42.633
All the insults hurt sometimes, because
of Yennefer’s many insecurities.

00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:46.133
I mean it is like something crawled
up your arses and died.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.933
We used to send texts to each other

00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:49.966
and I remember texting her going

00:01:49.966 --> 00:01:55.000
If I were to insult you, if
Jaskier were to insult Yennefer,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.353
what would be the most hurtful thing?
What would hurt her?

00:01:58.353 --> 00:02:00.333
And then I went to Lauren and was like

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:04.433
Look, when I’m adlibbing or improvising,
is it alright if I take this in a new direction?

00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:06.933
We wanted to show these
characters understood each other

00:02:06.933 --> 00:02:10.166
perhaps better than even they know

00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:15.000
and they have this innate ability of
being able to hurt each other emotionally.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.466
You know, once upon a time, I would
have used this opportunity

00:02:17.466 --> 00:02:20.066
to call you an empty, lonely,
power hungry she-demon. 

00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:22.026
There’s love there, deep down.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:26.433
But, they soon realise
that’s not enough.

00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:29.100
In the world that we’re experiencing,

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.780
in the Continent that is
collapsing around our ears,

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.800
two people who have lost something

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.333
are brought together by their own tragedies.

00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:41.600
It always feels light-hearted

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.533
and I think that’s what makes
them so strong as a couple,

00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:46.666
to watch rather so exciting.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.300
Hang on, what are you going to do?

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.100
What witches do best.
Make a potion.

00:02:53.853 --> 00:02:56.866
I always feel in incredibly good hands

00:02:56.866 --> 00:02:58.800
when Anya is on the set

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.333
and she’s just an absolute delight
and an incredible talent.

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:04.653
I’m so lucky to have worked with her.

00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:10.100
Chaos could never be done
with the likes of you,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.100
Yennefer of Vengerberg.

00:03:14.866 --> 00:03:18.186
Of that much, I am certain.

00:03:19.073 --> 00:03:21.033
So if it’s all the same to you.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.500
Goodbye.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.780
Good luck.

00:03:26.433 --> 00:03:28.753
Good riddance.

00:03:31.813 --> 00:03:33.173
Same to you.

